{"causes": ["The establishment of the Argead dynasty in Aigai provided the initial framework for a Macedonian kingdom.", "The ongoing need for a strong central authority to unite disparate Macedonian tribes and defend against external incursions necessitated a king.", "The patrilineal succession customs of the Argead house determined Alcetas I's claim to the throne following his father Aeropus I."], "effects": ["Alcetas I's reign ensured the continued succession of the Argead dynasty, maintaining a stable lineage for centuries.", "His rule contributed to the gradual consolidation of the Macedonian state during its formative period.", "The internal stability fostered under Alcetas I laid groundwork for future Macedonian expansion and influence in the Hellenic world."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "aeropus-i-of-macedon", "sourceName": "Aeropus I of Macedon", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "alcetas-i-of-macedon", "targetName": "Alcetas I of Macedon", "context": "Aeropus I of Macedon was the father of Alcetas I, establishing his dynastic claim to the Macedonian throne."}, {"sourceSlug": "alcetas-i-of-macedon", "sourceName": "Alcetas I of Macedon", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "aeropus-i-of-macedon", "targetName": "Aeropus I of Macedon", "context": "Alcetas I of Macedon succeeded his father, Aeropus I, as king of Macedon, continuing the Argead lineage."}, {"sourceSlug": "alcetas-i-of-macedon", "sourceName": "Alcetas I of Macedon", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "ancient-macedonia", "targetName": "Ancient Macedonia", "context": "Alcetas I's reign occurred within the geographic and political confines of Ancient Macedonia, centered around the region of Aigai."}, {"sourceSlug": "alcetas-i-of-macedon", "sourceName": "Alcetas I of Macedon", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "argead-dynasty", "targetName": "Argead Dynasty", "context": "Alcetas I transmitted the royal authority and lineage of the Argead Dynasty to his successor, Amyntas I, ensuring its continuity